A||N||3||Ozzy||Has any one...||||5||
Z||000000||Ozzy||04-09-2000||12:30 AM||||Hey folks...<P>I have been wrenching on th 'blue beast' today repairing the exhaust manifolds amongst other stuff. When I pulled the rear manifold (Firewall) I noticed that there was no stud on the bottom far right. Then the other night I read somewhere that "it is impossible to remove/install this stud without moving the air cond. compressor out of the way." The problem did not occur to me as I removed the manifold 'cause the last dude who worked on it put it in the "tOO hard basket" <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>I did manage to place the new stud and tighten it without moving the compressor but man, WHAT A PAIN!!!<P> I had to modify a thin flat box wrench by scalloping one side. This gave me  the extra rotation needed to get the next bite at the stud. After much patience and scratched arms I finally got it tightened up.<P>Ozzy||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||04-09-2000||07:34 AM||||I'm having a set out of my parts car ported/welded by Tom as we speak. I'm NOT looking forward to putting them in when he's done! Haven't decided yet if I'll attempt to do them myself or bring them to someone. I figure though that if I try and something goes wrong (broken stud,etc) at least I'll know versus picking up my car somewhere and have them say "your all set" and find out later the hard way that they f**ked up! I've gotten good tips on removing/installing from so many here...like you Ozzy! TKS||||reg||2
Z||000002||Ozzy||04-09-2000||12:29 PM||||Hey Gokart...<P>Overall, it is not that hard. Especially if you are only installing them. The main thing is "the right tool for the right job" I think. Good quality box wrenches and sockets for tough bolts etc...<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||04-09-2000||04:51 PM||||Thanks OZ. I got plenty of tools, but I'm worried about taking the old ones out of my GT when I get the set back from Tom. Ogre scared me enough when he said "there are only ugly and very ugly ways to get to those bolts". I'm scared I'm going to snap one. A couple did snap on the front set when I removed them from my parts car and I had them soaking in liquid wrench for a week before attempting! Maybe because that car hadn't been running in over 3 years they were more apt to break off!||||reg||14
